  "findings": [
    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "The new guard `if (slotEndTime.isAfter(workingHourEnd)) return false;` can reject or accept slots incorrectly if `slotEndTime` is derived from `slotStartTime.add(eventLength, \"minutes\")` in a different instant basis than `workingHourEnd`. The diff adds an end-boundary check but does not show any timezone or date alignment between the compared values, so a slot that should fit within the working window on the same local day may now be misclassified when `workingHourEnd` represents a local-day cutoff and `slotEndTime` is an instant derived from the start timestamp.",
